C = dict(id='GL-07', title='360-Degree Photography and Virtual Tours', group='Digital and Technology', level=3,
 summary='Capture, stitch and publish a safe, easy-to-use virtual tour of one real space, and prove that visitors can find their way around it.',
 outcomes=['Explain how a 360 image works and who gains from a virtual tour.', 'Capture a space on a steady stand with even light and overlap.', 'Analyse seams, load time and visitor scores to find what to fix.', 'Build a linked tour with captions, alt text and a floor map.', 'Judge the finished tour against rights, privacy and ease-of-use checks.'],
 task='Capture, build and publish a virtual tour of one real space with 6 to 10 linked spots.',
 cond='A phone or low-cost 360 camera, a steady stand, a free stitching and tour tool, a free image editor, written permission from the space owner, a mentor and a peer circle. About 10 weeks part-time.',
 std='Written permission held; faces, number plates and private papers hidden; every spot has a caption and alt text; the first spot loads in under 5 seconds on slow data; ten visitors give an average ease score of 4 out of 5 or better.',
 who='Small-business owners, estate and hospitality staff, school and college learners, freelancers.', req='A phone and a space you may photograph.',
 safety='Get written permission from the owner of the space and from anyone who appears. Blur faces, number plates and private papers.',
 mods=[
 ('Why a tour, and for whom', 'A tour is useful only when a real person uses it to decide something. Start with the user, not the camera.', ['A 360 image is a full sphere of view; the viewer looks around on a screen.', 'List five places where a tour helps a buyer decide: classroom, shop, guest room, workshop, hall.', 'Ask the owner what a visitor should see first and what must stay hidden.', 'Write the plan: 6 to 10 spots, a hide list, and how the link will be shared.'], 'A guest house owner wants fewer phone questions. Plan: 8 spots (entrance, 3 rooms, kitchen, garden, dining, road view); hide list: guest belongings and the office desk.', 'Choose one space, get written permission and write the one-page plan.', 'Permission on file; 6 to 10 spots listed; hide list written.'),
 ('Rights, privacy and access', 'A tour can harm people if it shows what it should not. Decide the rules before you press the shutter.', ['Permission from the owner and from any person who can be recognised.', 'Blur faces, number plates, screens and papers; remove street-door codes.', 'Write alt text for each spot so blind and low-vision visitors can follow the tour.', 'Keep a short consent note and a takedown contact on the tour page.'], 'A hall has a notice board with phone numbers. The hide list says blur the board; the checker confirms it in spot 4.', 'Write the hide list and the alt-text style (one sentence: where, what, what to do next).', 'Hide list covers every spot; alt-text style agreed with the mentor.'),
 ('Capture technique', 'Good capture saves hours of repair later. Keep height, level and light steady.', ['Camera at eye level on a stand, the same height at every spot.', 'Spots about a step and a half apart in rooms, further in halls.', 'Step out of view or use a timer; check mirrors and glass for your reflection.', 'In bright rooms take two exposures so light can be balanced later.'], 'A room with a bright window: one shot exposed for the room, one for the window. Merged later, both the sofa and the garden are visible.', 'Walk the space with a floor plan, mark spots and capture them all.', 'All spots captured at one height with overlap; no person or stand visible in the raw files.'),
 ('Stitching and fixing', 'Stitching joins overlapping pictures into one sphere. Seams and a tilted horizon are the usual faults.', ['Check seams on straight lines such as door frames and tables.', 'Level the horizon; fix colour so adjacent spots match.', 'Retouch the stand out of the floor.', 'Log each fault and the fix: a short table beats memory.'], 'Of 8 spots, 2 show a bent door frame at the seam: 2 of 8 is 25% needing a fix. After re-stitching with more overlap, 0 of 8 fail.', 'Stitch all spots and keep a fault log.', 'Fault log complete; no visible seam error in the final images.'),
 ('Building the tour', 'A tour is a path, not a pile of pictures. Links, captions and a map guide the viewer.', ['Choose the start spot: the one that answers the visitor\'s first question.', 'Add arrows between spots; keep each spot to two or three links.', 'One caption and one alt text per spot; add a simple floor map.', 'Compress images so the tour opens on a phone.'], '8 images at 6 MB are 48 MB. Compressed to 1.5 MB each they are 12 MB, about 48 seconds on a 2 Mbit/s link if loaded at once; loading the first spot only takes under 5 seconds.', 'Build the draft tour and test it on a phone with slow data and on a computer.', 'First spot loads in under 5 seconds; every spot has a caption and alt text.'),
 ('Viewing circle and testing', 'Fresh eyes find problems you cannot see. Watch people use it without helping them.', ['Ask three peers to find the kitchen without any help.', 'Record where they hesitate, get lost or leave.', 'Count load time, number of spots and confusing links.', 'Ask a mentor with photo or property experience to check light, seams and rights.'], 'Three of four peers cannot find the garden: the link is hidden behind a plant. Move the arrow, retest: all four find it in under 20 seconds.', 'Run the viewing circle and write down five fixes.', 'Five fixes listed, ranked and dated.'),
 ('Measure and decide', 'A tour earns its keep only if people use it. Measure and then decide: publish, improve, or keep private.', ['Ask the owner and ten visitors to score ease and truth to the real place from 1 to 5.', 'Average the scores: sum divided by number of people.', 'Count views and enquiries for two weeks.', 'Write three lessons learned and one clear decision.'], 'Ten visitors give ease scores totalling 42, an average of 4.2; truth-to-place totals 45, average 4.5. Decision: publish, and fix the one slow spot.', 'Collect scores, calculate averages and write the decision note.', 'Scores calculated correctly; decision backed by numbers.'),
 ('Review room and next 90 days', 'Show your work, learn from others, and plan the next step.', ['Present the space, plan, tour, scores and decision in five minutes.', 'Give two peers written feedback: one strength, one fix.', 'Get a short written note from one real user.', 'Share a checklist or template so the next learner starts higher.'], 'A learner shares a hide-list template; two later learners reuse it and credits are recorded.', 'Present, give feedback and write your 90-day plan.', 'Two peer reviews given; 90-day plan has dates and a measure.')],
 quiz=[('What is a 360 image?', 'A full-sphere picture the viewer can look around on a screen.'), ('Why keep the camera at one height?', 'So spots match and the tour feels steady.'), ('What must you hold before capturing a private space?', 'Written permission from the owner.'), ('What is stitching?', 'Joining overlapping pictures into one sphere.'), ('Why write alt text?', 'So blind and low-vision visitors can follow the tour.'), ('Why compress images?', 'So the tour loads on a phone with slow data.'), ('What must be blurred or hidden?', 'Faces, number plates, screens, papers and codes.'), ('Why test on slow data?', 'Many visitors have slow links; waiting makes them leave.'), ('How do you calculate an average score?', 'Add all scores and divide by the number of people.'), ('Name three decisions after testing.', 'Publish, improve, or keep private.')],
 rubric=[('Permission and privacy', 'Permission held; hide list followed', 'Also a takedown contact and consent note'), ('Capture quality', 'Even height, light and overlap', 'Fault log shows fixes and no repeats'), ('Tour design', 'Clear path with captions and alt text', 'Map, fast load and tested by strangers'), ('Evidence of use', 'Ten scores and averages correct', 'Views and enquiries counted over two weeks'), ('Reflection', 'Three lessons written', 'Lessons changed the next plan with dates')],
 jobs=[('Virtual tour photographer', 'Captures and builds tours for local businesses'), ('Property or hospitality marketing assistant', 'Adds tours to listings'), ('School or museum digital assistant', 'Makes accessible tours of spaces'), ('Freelance tour builder', 'Sells tours to small firms')],
 next='Virtual Event Planning; Virtual Interior Design Consulting; Online Car Dealership Operations.',
 local='Image and privacy rules differ by place: ask whether recognisable people, children or private homes need extra consent.',
 evidence='Your evidence: permission note, hide list, fault log, published tour link, ten visitor scores, decision note and 90-day plan.',
 ladder=[('Basics of looking around', 'Explain a 360 image and view one tour. Notes: no tools needed; use a free sample tour and describe what helps and what confuses.'), ('Awareness of rights', 'Know consent, privacy and accessibility basics. Notes: role-play asking an owner for permission.'), ('Capture and build one tour', 'This course. Notes: learners finish a six-to-ten-spot tour with testing.'), ('Tours for paying clients', 'Quote, schedule and deliver a tour for a small firm. Notes: introduce pricing in your own currency and a simple contract.'), ('Specialist tours', 'Tours with floor plans, measurements and accessibility audits. Notes: add measured plans and an access report.'), ('Advanced studio lead', 'Lead a small team and a quality system. Notes: set standards, train juniors, review rights files.'), ('Super expert', 'Set method and train trainers. Notes: publish templates, mentor others and review the course yearly.')])
